I would make the opening video the defining feature of the website.

How the parallax should work:

1. The visitor enters the homepage and sees a full-screen horizontal video.
2. The video is positioned as a background layer inside a pinned hero section.
3. The user scrolls down.
4. The hero stays temporarily pinned while the video subtly shifts and scales.
5. The headline and tagline move at a different speed, creating depth.
6. Once the animation finishes, the next section enters naturally.

The video itself should remain a horizontal 16:9 composition. It should not become a horizontal-scrolling gallery.

Suggested video direction:

- Bottles resting in shallow beach water.
- Slow-moving foam interacting with the glass.
- Sand subtly shifting beneath the water.
- Light reflecting off the bottle shoulders.
- Botanical shadows moving across the background.
- Macro details of condensation and glass.
- Muted, earthy colour grading.

The camera should feel almost stationary. The environment creates the movement.

## 05. Responsive design

The desktop website is the primary art direction, but mobile must receive its own considered composition.

| Component         | Desktop         | Mobile                       |
| ----------------- | --------------- | ---------------------------- |
| Navigation        | Horizontal      | Compact menu                 |
| Hero              | Full viewport   | Full viewport, cropped video |
| Product grid      | 2 columns       | 1 column                     |
| Editorial imagery | Full-width      | Edge-to-edge                 |
| Typography        | Large editorial | Fluid responsive sizing      |
| Footer            | Multi-column    | Stacked                      |
| Cart              | Side drawer     | Full-screen drawer           |

The video must have a poster image and mobile-optimised alternative. Respect reduced-motion settings and provide a static alternative for users who disable motion.

## 06. Technical build requirements

My recommendation is to build this as a lightweight, responsive website rather than a complex application.

Suggested technology:

- Frontend: React / Next.js.
- Styling: Tailwind CSS or custom CSS.
- Animation: GSAP ScrollTrigger for the pinned parallax hero, with lightweight CSS transitions elsewhere.
- Ecommerce: Shopify integration or another supported South African ecommerce provider.
- Content management: Editable product information, pricing, photography and page content.
- Hosting: Vercel or an equivalent production hosting service.

Important: Google AI should build the actual working website, not simply return a static design or screenshot.

